": "contract", "label": "New provider numbers", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "$500,000 or more within a year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.47, 0.66, 0.77]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "5 brand-new provider numbers took 500,000 dollars or more within about a year.", "t0": 55.88, "t1": 60.19, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "New provider numbers", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "$500,000 or more within a year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.43, 0.84, 1.22, 1.53, 1.79, 2.01, 2.23, 2.53, 2.79, 2.93, 3.15, 3.4, 3.64, 3.73]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "That’s the classic shape of a billing mill, a fake clinic built to bill fast.", "t0": 60.31, "t1": 64.49, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the classic shape of a billing mill"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.38, 0.8, 1.09, 1.19, 1.26, 1.55, 2.0, 2.16, 2.41, 2.78, 3.05, 3.19, 3.42]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Or of an old practice re-formed as a new company.", "t0": 64.61, "t1": 67.19, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the classic shape of a billing mill"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.29, 0.41, 0.64, 1.12, 1.57, 1.68, 1.76, 1.92]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The third lead: 32 groups the City pays also bill Medicaid themselves.", "t0": 67.41, "t1": 71.73, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The City", "sub": "pays a grant"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "The organization", "sub": "provides care"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Medicaid", "sub": "pays for care too"}], "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.41, 1.22, 1.71, 1.98, 2.11, 2.39, 2.76, 3.09, 3.31, 3.69]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[4]", "notEstablished[8]"], "text": "23 of the 32 are confirmed by an address or an officer; 9 match by name alone.", "t0": 71.85, "t1": 76.63, "shot": "b9n", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["confirmed by a second record", "23"], "b": ["matched by name alone", "9"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.53, 0.6, 0.71, 1.14, 1.27, 1.71, 1.85, 1.92, 2.28, 2.39, 2.5, 3.49, 3.82, 4.09, 4.23, 4.43]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "For 7, Medicaid money is new or tripled since 2021.", "t0": 76.75, "t1": 80.59, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The City", "sub": "pays a grant"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "The organization", "sub": "provides care"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Medicaid", "sub": "pays for care too"}], "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.99, 1.46, 1.75, 1.95, 2.2, 2.33, 2.77, 3.02, 3.33]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "How much in 2024?", "t0": 80.71, "t1": 82.12, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The City", "sub": "pays a grant"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "The organization", "sub": "provides care"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Medicaid", "sub": "pays for care too"}], "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.38, 0.49, 0.74]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "21.4 million dollars.", "t0": 82.12, "t1": 83.94, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$21.4 million", "label": "from Medicaid to 7 City-funded groups, 2024"}, "emph": ["21.4"], "wt": [0.04, 0.53, 0.77, 1.0, 1.32]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "City pay to the same 7 rose too, from 30 million dollars to 46.7 million.", "t0": 84.46, "t1": 89.87, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City pay, fiscal 2022", "$30.0 million"], "b": ["City pay, fiscal 2026", "$46.7 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.57, 0.68, 0.79, 1.13, 1.46, 1.82, 2.57, 2.82, 3.08, 3.35, 3.67, 3.8, 4.3, 4.56, 4.86]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Did one cost get billed to both? Nothing shows that.", "t0": 89.99, "t1": 92.8, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City pay, fiscal 2022", "$30.0 million"], "b": ["City pay, fiscal 2026", "$46.7 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.41, 0.67, 0.84, 1.09, 1.22, 1.9, 2.21, 2.49]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "The fourth lead: in 2023, local billers got 2,174 dollars per enrolled resident.", "t0": 93.02, "t1": 99.43, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["California, 2023", "$1,482"], "b": ["San Francisco, 2023", "$2,174"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.45, 1.3, 1.46, 1.75, 2.33, 2.6, 2.89, 3.1, 3.34, 3.81, 3.99, 4.24, 4.76, 5.15, 5.32, 5.73]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "California: 1,482. 1.47 times as much.", "t0": 99.55, "t1": 104.35, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["California, 2023", "$1,482"], "b": ["San Francisco, 2023", "$2,174"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.93, 1.11, 1.44, 1.63, 1.89, 3.04, 3.24, 3.51, 3.73, 3.99, 4.28, 4.4]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Why so high? A big university hospital and national labs are registered here.", "t0": 104.47, "t1": 108.67, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "City government’s own billers", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "51% of the San Francisco total"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.46, 1.31, 1.46, 1.66, 2.16, 2.6, 2.76, 3.13, 3.42, 3.54, 3.99]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "And City government itself took 51 percent.", "t0": 108.79, "t1": 111.1, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "City government’s own billers", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "51% of the San Francisco total"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.42, 0.73, 1.11, 1.36, 1